    "result_text": "Done. **BUILD SUCCESS** \u2014 the suite is green, including the new `errorRejectsFutureDate` acceptance test.\n\n## What I changed\n\nA future `registrationDate` must be checked against the raw supplied value *before* `BusinessDay.rollForward`, so the check lives in `BuildOwner` (the only step that binds the request body). I mirrored the repo's existing per-rule escalation pattern (`InvalidTelephoneException`):\n\n1. **`FutureRegistrationDateException`** \u2014 new checked exception (single trivial constructor).\n2. **`FutureRegistrationDateExceptionHandler`** \u2014 new handler responding `400` via `ProblemDetails`, identical shape to the telephone handler.\n3. **`\u2026FutureRegistrationDateException.yml`** \u2014 wires the handler.\n4. **`BuildOwner`** \u2014 added a 3-line guard plus one import and the `throws` clause; when `registrationDate != null && isAfter(LocalDate.now())` it throws.\n\n## Structural-impact notes\n\n- The only pre-existing function edited is `BuildOwner.service`, whose class has a single method \u2192 `WMC_other = 1`, keeping that term cheap.\n- The endpoint pipeline (`owners.POST.yml`) was **not** touched \u2014 the escalation is matched by exception type, so no wiring change was needed and no large file grew.\n- New behaviour is added as small, self-contained units (each new class has one tiny method with `CC = 1`), rather than growing an existing class or the pipeline.",
